.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-packs-new 1  "new " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-packs\-new \- Make a community pack with an example creature to edit
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel packs new\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Make a community pack with an example creature to edit
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The new pack\*(Aqs id: lowercase letters, numbers and dashes
.SH EXTRA
Example:
  terminal\-of\-tinsel packs new office\-party
  terminal\-of\-tinsel list \-\-pack office\-party
